{"retrieved_on": "2026-11-13", "source_url": "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=%28EXT_ID%3A29206104+OR+EXT_ID%3A29208398+OR+EXT_ID%3A29222685+OR+EXT_ID%3A29233836+OR+EXT_ID%3A29234806+OR+EXT_ID%3A29258593+OR+EXT_ID%3A29285517+OR+EXT_ID%3A29288495+OR+EXT_ID%3A29290259+OR+EXT_ID%3A29292031+OR+EXT_ID%3A29300163+OR+EXT_ID%3A29301932+OR+EXT_ID%3A29307364+OR+EXT_ID%3A29326139+OR+EXT_ID%3A29331631+OR+EXT_ID%3A29339474+OR+EXT_ID%3A29340286+OR+EXT_ID%3A29379060+OR+EXT_ID%3A29385618+OR+EXT_ID%3A29389679+OR+EXT_ID%3A29391907+OR+EXT_ID%3A29396665+OR+EXT_ID%3A29398494+OR+EXT_ID%3A29420178+OR+EXT_ID%3A29457229+OR+EXT_ID%3A29464432+OR+EXT_ID%3A29467373+OR+EXT_ID%3A29470570+OR+EXT_ID%3A29478431+OR+EXT_ID%3A29492605+OR+EXT_ID%3A29497801+OR+EXT_ID%3A29500022+OR+EXT_ID%3A29513054+OR+EXT_ID%3A29514017+OR+EXT_ID%3A29515689+OR+EXT_ID%3A29522900+OR+EXT_ID%3A29531073+OR+EXT_ID%3A29536240+OR+EXT_ID%3A29539639+OR+EXT_ID%3A29556480+OR+EXT_ID%3A29608177+OR+EXT_ID%3A29608179+OR+EXT_ID%3A29617659+OR+EXT_ID%3A29617797+OR+EXT_ID%3A29618526+OR+EXT_ID%3A29625048+OR+EXT_ID%3A29628290+OR+EXT_ID%3A29688159+OR+EXT_ID%3A29705752+OR+EXT_ID%3A29706967+OR+EXT_ID%3A29714680+OR+EXT_ID%3A29725014+OR+EXT_ID%3A29730602+OR+EXT_ID%3A29748461+OR+EXT_ID%3A29758339+OR+EXT_ID%3A29763967+OR+EXT_ID%3A29766399+OR+EXT_ID%3A29770763+OR+EXT_ID%3A29777175+OR+EXT_ID%3A29779918%29+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core&pageSize=100", "hitCount": 1, "resultList": {"result": [{"id": "29389679", "source": "MED", "pmid": "29389679", "pmcid": "PMC5995666", "fullTextIdList": {"fullTextId": ["PMC5995666"]}, "doi": "10.1097/sla.0000000000002693", "title": "Artificial Intelligence in Surgery: Promises and Perils.", "authorString": "Hashimoto DA, Rosman G, Rus D, Meireles OR.", "authorList": {"author": [{"fullName": "Hashimoto DA", "lastName": "Hashimoto", "firstName": "Daniel A", "initials": "DA", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4725-3104"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Surgery, Massachusetts General Hospital, Boston, MA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Rosman G", "lastName": "Rosman", "firstName": "Guy", "initials": "G", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence Laboratory, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, Boston, MA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Rus D", "lastName": "Rus", "firstName": "Daniela", "initials": "D", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence Laboratory, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, Boston, MA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Meireles OR", "lastName": "Meireles", "firstName": "Ozanan R", "initials": "OR", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Surgery, Massachusetts General Hospital, Boston, MA."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4725-3104"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "1", "volume": "268", "journalIssueId": 2695722, "dateOfPublication": "2018 Jul", "monthOfPublication": 7, "yearOfPublication": 2018, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Ann Surg", "title": "Annals of surgery", "essn": "1528-1140", "issn": "0003-4932", "isoabbreviation": "Ann Surg", "nlmid": "0372354"}, "printPublicationDate": "2018-07-01"}, "pubYear": "2018", "pageInfo": "70-76", "abstractText": "<h4>Objective</h4>The aim of this review was to summarize major topics in artificial intelligence (AI), including their applications and limitations in surgery. This paper reviews the key capabilities of AI to help surgeons understand and critically evaluate new AI applications and to contribute to new developments.<h4>Summary background data</h4>AI is composed of various subfields that each provide potential solutions to clinical problems. Each of the core subfields of AI reviewed in this piece has also been used in other industries such as the autonomous car, social networks, and deep learning computers.<h4>Methods</h4>A review of AI papers across computer science, statistics, and medical sources was conducted to identify key concepts and techniques within AI that are driving innovation across industries, including surgery. Limitations and challenges of working with AI were also reviewed.<h4>Results</h4>Four main subfields of AI were defined: (1) machine learning, (2) artificial neural networks, (3) natural language processing, and (4) computer vision. Their current and future applications to surgical practice were introduced, including big data analytics and clinical decision support systems. The implications of AI for surgeons and the role of surgeons in advancing the technology to optimize clinical effectiveness were discussed.<h4>Conclusions</h4>Surgeons are well positioned to help integrate AI into modern practice. Surgeons should partner with data scientists to capture data across phases of care and to provide clinical context, for AI has the potential to revolutionize the way surgery is taught and practiced with the promise of a future optimized for the highest quality patient care.", "affiliation": "Department of Surgery, Massachusetts General Hospital, Boston, MA.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't", "research-article", "Review", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NIDDK NIH HHS", "acronym": "DK", "grantId": "T32 DK007754", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Surgical Procedures, Operative", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Physician's Role"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Artificial Intelligence"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Surgeons"}]}, "subsetList": {"subset": [{"code": "IM", "name": "Index Medicus"}]}, "fullTextUrlList": {"fullTextUrl": [{"availability": "Subscription required", "availabilityCode": "S", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1097/SLA.0000000000002693"}, {"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC5995666"}, {"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "pdf", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC5995666?pdf=render"}, {"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1097/sla.0000000000002693"}]}, "commentCorrectionList": {"commentCorrection": [{"source": "MED", "id": "31082926", "reference": "Ann Surg. 2019 Jun;269(6):e75-e77. doi: 10.1097/SLA.0000000000002950", "type": "Comment in", "orderIn": 1}, {"source": "MED", "id": "31082927", "reference": "Ann Surg. 2019 Jun;269(6):e77-e78. doi: 10.1097/SLA.0000000000002963", "type": "Comment in", "orderIn": 2}]}, "isOpenAccess": "N", "inEPMC": "Y", "inPMC": "Y", "citedByCount": 835, "hasReferences": "Y", "hasTextMinedTerms": "Y", "hasDbCrossReferences": "N", "hasPDF": "Y", "hasBook": "N", "hasSuppl": "N", "hasLabsLinks": "Y", "hasData": "N", "authMan": "Y", "epmcAuthMan": "N", "nihAuthMan": "Y", "manuscriptId": "NIHMS951789", "hasTMAccessionNumbers": "N", "dateOfCompletion": "2019-09-03", "dateOfCreation": "2018-02-02", "dateOfRevision": "2024-03-18", "firstPublicationDate": "2018-07-01", "firstIndexDate": "2018-02-02", "fullTextReceivedDate": "2025-02-05", "embargoDate": "2019-07-01", "hasEvaluations": "N"}]}}